Ladybird uses a nonempty option label for display and otherwise
shows the option text. Blink’s HTMLOptionElement::DisplayLabel,
WebKit’s HTMLOptionElement::displayLabel, and Gecko’s
HTMLOptionElement::GetRenderedLabel make this distinction.
An empty label attribute still reflects as an empty string
through the IDL getter.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 gave equal
widths to otherwise identical selects with absent and empty
labels. Changing an option label from a nonempty string to an empty
one also restored its text.
